Hi <%= @first_name %>,

The Airtable sync for <%= @event.name %> has failed <%= pluralize(@failures, "time") %> in a row.
This usually means Airtable is rate limiting the base or having an outage, so
Attend is still retrying every 5 minutes. You don't need to change anything
unless it keeps failing.

You're getting this because you were the last person to save the Airtable
settings for this event.

What Airtable said:

<%= @error_message %>

If it doesn't recover, check that nothing else is sending a lot of requests to
the same base, and look at https://status.airtable.com.

<%= @integrations_url %>

<% if @last_synced_at %>
Last successful sync was <%= @last_synced_at.strftime("%b %-d, %Y at %-I:%M %p %Z") %> -- Airtable still shows that data.
<% else %>
This integration has never synced successfully.
<% end %>

We'll only email again if it fails for a while after its next successful sync.

If you're not the right person for this any more, just reply and we'll sort it out.
